WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.295
"Resveratrol Tested for Alzheimer’s, Arthritis, and Osteoporosis"

00:00:07.434 --> 00:00:09.780
Does resveratrol help
with inflammation?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:12.720
In humans, the evidence
of an anti-inflammatory effect

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:14.100
is sparse and conflicting.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.660
About half of the studies show

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.160
a modest
anti-inflammatory effect,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.020
but the other half
failed to find any.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.720
The proof, however,
is in the pudding.

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.080
What about clinical effects
on inflammatory disease?

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.800
In rats and mice,

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.140
resveratrol can help
ameliorate the effects

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.240
of experimentally-induced
periodontitis,

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:34.740
the inflammatory gum disease.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:37.320
However, it appears
to have no effect

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.360
on the progression
of chronic periodontitis

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.620
in human sufferers.

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:44.340
Resveratrol may help with
the inflammatory bowel disease

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:45.540
ulcerative colitis, though.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.580
A pilot study
of 500 milligrams a day

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.960
of resveratrol for six weeks

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.900
resulted in significantly
decreased disease activity

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.780
and elevated quality of life
compared to placebo.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.720
What about inflammatory
joint disease?

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.000
One pilot study
of 500 milligrams a day

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.040
of resveratrol
for knee osteoarthritis

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.200
found a decrease in pain
within a month,

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:05.880
but there was no control group;

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.620
so, the change can't
really be attributed

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.940
to starting the supplements.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:11.040
However, a second pilot study,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:13.260
a randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial,

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:15.840
found that the same dose
taken as an "add on"

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:19.020
to an anti-inflammatory drug
significantly improved

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:20.520
pain and function
within a month

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.100
in mild-to-moderate
knee osteoarthritis sufferers,

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.720
more than adding a placebo.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.960
The one clinical trial
of rheumatoid arthritis

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.240
had a control group,
but no placebo,

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:32.640
though there were
objective signs of improvement

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.820
in disease activity after
taking 1000 milligrams a day

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:36.720
for three months.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.180
Resveratrol may also be
beneficial

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:40.920
to combat menopausal symptoms.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:44.340
Resveratrol has
some estrogenic activity.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:47.040
Although it doesn't appear
to help with hormonal migraines,

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.640
it does appear to help
with a couple symptoms of PCOS,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:52.140
polycystic ovary syndrome.

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.040
RESHAW—Resveratrol
for Healthy Ageing in Women—

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.960
is the longest study of effects

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.960
of resveratrol supplementation
in postmenopausal women.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.360
Those randomized
to 75 milligrams

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:04.740
of resveratrol twice a day

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.800
suffered significantly fewer
physical menopausal symptoms,

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:09.180
including aches and pains,

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.460
and a general improvement
in overall well-being

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:12.960
compared to placebo.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.260
The RESHAW study also looked
at bone loss prevention.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:18.600
Unfortunately,
though animal studies

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.280
show protective effects
on bone tissue,

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:22.080
a meta-analysis
of human studies

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:24.480
on resveratrol supplementation
to improve bone quality

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.720
found no significant effect
on bone health markers

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.100
or bone mineral density

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:32.580
of the spine, hip,
or overall skeleton.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.480
A similar story was found
for cognitive effects.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.480
Most studies on resveratrol
for brain function

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.580
in animal models
show positive outcomes,

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.040
but meta-analyses
of human studies show

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:45.720
no significant effect
on memory,

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.820
processing speed,
executive function,

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.680
or global
cognitive performance,

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.860
which led reviewers to suggest
that resveratrol may be

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:55.620
a "cognitive enhancer
for mice only."

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:59.580
Most human cognition studies
found no effect

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:02.340
or mixed results—higher
performance on some tasks,

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:04.260
but lower performance on others,
compared to placebo,

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.900
resulting in
a "lack of interpretable

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:08.040
cognitive effects."

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.680
Some have suggested
the discrepancy

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:12.660
between the animal models
and the clinical data

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:15.060
is that the rodents
were massively dosed,

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.520
up to a gram per kilogram
of body weight a day,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.080
which would be
like giving people

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:19.980
an entire bottle

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.440
of high-dose resveratrol
supplements at once.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.560
Or, ironically,
it could be the opposite,

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.140
where the doses researchers
gave people were too large.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.880
A dose-response study

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.860
found that human
cerebral blood flow

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.000
was maximally boosted

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:35.580
by the lowest dose
of resveratrol tested,

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:36.960
seventy-five milligrams a day.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:39.480
So, when the RESHAW study
was developed,

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:42.000
that was the dose they used,
given twice a day.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.760
RESHAW was primarily designed
to test the effects

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:46.680
of resveratrol
on cognitive performance.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:50.640
Interim analyses at 14 weeks
and a year looked promising,

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.800
leading the researchers
to conclude that their findings

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.955
"support the adoption
of resveratrol

00:03:54.955 --> 00:03:56.520
as a low-cost,
effective intervention

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.840
to help counteract the age-

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.360
and menopause-related
accelerated cognitive decline

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.440
in our ageing population."

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.920
However, by the end
of the two-year study,

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.720
it's not clear
if the apparent benefit

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:07.800
in overall cognition

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.680
survives adjustment
for multiple comparisons,

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:13.680
meaning there were so many
cognitive outcomes tested

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:15.420
that the few treatment
differences

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.580
may well have arisen
through chance.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.840
What about cognitive benefit
for those who really need it?

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.540
Observational studies
find wine drinkers

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.860
tend to get less dementia,

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.920
but it's hard to disentangle
the social, cognitive,

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.120
and personality factors

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.280
that accompany
a wine drinking habit.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:36.000
So, researchers decided
to put resveratrol to the test

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.740
for Alzheimer's disease.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:40.620
A randomized double-blind,
placebo-controlled pilot

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:43.920
out of Cornell in 2006
kicked things off with a bang.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.380
Patients with mild-to-moderate
Alzheimer's disease

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.300
who were randomized
to a 5 milligram

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.460
resveratrol concoction
twice a day

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.800
ended up with significantly
better cognition

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:54.540
after three months
compared to placebo.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:58.080
There was a greater
than expected deterioration

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.640
in the placebo group, though,

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:02.040
suggesting that this may
have just been a fluke,

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:04.860
especially since an attempt
to replicate the study

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.340
with the same dose for a year
failed to find any effects

00:05:08.340 --> 00:05:09.780
of statistical significance.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:13.320
Maybe the researchers just
didn't use a high enough dose?

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.240
More than a hundred patients

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:16.560
with mild to moderate
Alzheimer's

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:17.580
were randomized to placebo

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.800
or an escalating dose
of resveratrol

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:21.600
starting at a hundred times
the dose

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:23.760
of the previous study—
500 milligrams once a day

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.760
and ending at a 1000 milligrams
twice a day.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.020
After a year,

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:31.200
there were no significant
improvements in cognition

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:33.300
or the performance of activities
of daily living

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.800
compared to placebo.

00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:39.600
Instead, there was
a significant acceleration

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:42.240
of brain volume loss.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:43.380
At the end of the study,

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.960
there was triple
the brain volume loss

00:05:45.960 --> 00:05:49.080
(3 percent versus 1 percent)
in the resveratrol group.

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.620
And the only other randomized,
double-blind,

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.940
placebo-controlled trial to date

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:55.260
found the same thing:

00:05:55.260 --> 00:05:57.300
no significant
cognitive benefits

00:05:57.300 --> 00:06:00.540
and the same tripling
of age-related brain shrinkage.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.440
The authors tried to somehow
spin this as a positive,

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:07.740
like hey—maybe that's just
decreased brain swelling,

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:10.020
but as a team
of researchers wrote

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:12.000
in an understatement
of the year,

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.880
"It is difficult
to reconcile these effects

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:16.920
as potentially beneficial."

